//
// hangar.map — the cinematic-demo's hangar.
//
// The layout is a 200×200 unit room with a 30×30 raised metal pad in the
// centre for the Interceptor. Walls/floor carry surface id 0 (stone);
// the pad carries surface id 1 (metal). kiln_map's current parser tags
// every worldspawn brush with surface=0 (see kiln_map.c:182), so the
// surface id distinction is currently *authored-only*; the cinematic
// uses surface for an audio shader ("step_metal" vs "step_stone") that
// is played by player footsteps via kiln_surface_play_footstep. The pad
// geometry is what gives the goblin a different footstep SFX as he walks
// across it.
//
// Brushes are 6-plane AABBs (each face uses 3 coplanar plane points).
// kiln_map reduces each brush to its AABB for collision and builds 6
// parallelogram faces for rendering, which is exactly the right shape
// for these rectangular rooms.
//
// Entity spawns:
//   info_player_start -> goblin's start position (the captain stands here)
//   info_droid        -> service droid, reads "radius" and "phase" from dict
//   info_alien        -> approaching alien, reads "path" and "speed" from dict
//
// The Interceptor and goblin are placed by code (not by the map).

{
"classname" "worldspawn"
